QuestGuidance.Register("en",368,{
[11745]="7004E4CF\n1\tSpeak with Kunchat to enter Instance: The Lone Dwarf\tAkh-gulûkh has asked you to join him and the other Jangovar leaders inside the Utterby Town Hall. You should speak with Kunchat and enter Instance: The Lone Dwarf.\n2\tTalk to Lord Náin\tLord Náin is outside Utterby. You should talk to Lord Náin.\n",
[11746]="7001B617\n1\tClaim the Entrance Hall\tIn order to secure the Tower, the Entrance Hall must first be claimed.\n2\tClaim the Audience Chamber\tThe Entrance Hall is secure, and Sigileth will ensure nothing enters from behind you. The next target is the Audience Chamber across the hall.\n3\tClaim the Lower Mustering Hall\tWith the Entrance Hall and Audience Chamber claimed, you may begin to climb the Tower and seek to claim the Lower Mustering Hall.\n4\tClaim the Upper Mustering Hall\tThe Upper Mustering Hall is directly above the Lower...with it claimed, the Enemy will be confused and any reinforcements poorly armed.\n5\tClaim the Armoury\tWith the Mustering Halls claimed, it is time to take the Armoury and reclaim Zigilburk.\n6\tClaim the Armoury\tWith the Mustering Halls claimed, it is time to take the Armoury and reclaim Zigilburk. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[11747]="70029FC6\n1\tComplete 'The Battle in the Tower' in a raid group\tThe Enemy is entrenched within the Tower of Dol Guldur. It is time to strike them at their heart.\n",
[11748]="70058BC5\n1\tFind and aid Dréri with 'Death's Breath'\030Find and aid Mézto with 'Vengeance in Kind'\030Find and aid Órug with 'Engines of Destruction'\tDréri, Mézto, and Órug can be found among the forces of the Gabil'akkâ at Azgh-buzru. Náin the Slakeless has commanded you to rally with his forces at Azgh-buzru, the war-fell and aid them in overcoming the forces of Mount Gundabad.\n2\tTalk to Náin the Slakeless at Drenghól\tNáin the Slakeless can be found at Drenghól in the War of Three Peaks. You have aided Dréri, Mézto, and Órug at Azgh-buzru. You should report to Náin and inform him of your success.\n3\tAid Náin the Slakeless with 'A Master of Two Minds'\030Aid Órug with 'The Lieutenants of Gorgar'\030Aid Dréri with 'No Quarter for the Captured'\030Aid Mézto with 'To Stoke A Cold Fire'\tNáin the Slakeless, Dréri, Mézto, and Órug can be found at Drenghól in the War of Three Peaks. Náin the Slakeless has ordered you to press the attack on the garrison at Bagûd-mekhem. You should speak to Náin the Slakeless, Dréri, Mézto, and Órug and aid them.\n4\tTalk to Náin the Slakeless at Drenghól\tNáin the Slakeless can be found at Drenghól in the War of Three Peaks. You have aided Náin the Slakeless and the dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ in overcoming the garrison at Bagûd-mekhem. You should report to Náin with news of your victory at Bagûd-mekhem.\n",
[11749]="70027A69\n1\tComplete Battle of Dol Baran\tCaptain Féarn awaits your attention atop Dol Baran. You should speak to Captain Féarn when you are ready to defend against the Dunlendings' assault.\n2\tTalk to Captain Féarn atop Dol Baran\tCaptain Féarn awaits you atop Dol Baran. You should speak with Captain Féarn regarding the victory you recently achieved there.\n",
[11750]="70019013\n1\tTalk to Belvagor and begin the defence of Lothlórien\tBelvagor is in Caras Galadhon, waiting for you to gather allies and speak to him to begin the defence of Lothlórien.\n2\tTalk to Belvagor at Caras Galadhon\tBelvagor is waiting to speak with you in Caras Galadhon about your defence of Lothlórien from the Orcs.\n",
[11751]="7002CB2A\n1\tTravel to Ost Celebrant\tOst Celebrant is the large fortress in south-east Parth Celebrant. Doron wishes to meet you on the bridge at Ost Celebrant.\n2\tOst Celebrant is the large fortress in south-east Parth Celebrant. Doron hopes to aid you by directing your assault as you move towards the heart of the ruins.\t\n3\tOst Celebrant is the large fortress in south-east Parth Celebrant. Doron hopes to aid you by directing your assault as you move towards the heart of the ruins.\t\n4\tTalk to Doron\030Summon Doron\tYou should speak with Doron regarding your assault on Ost Celebrant.\n5\tTalk to Doron at the Field of Celebrant\tDoron is among his men at the Field of Celebrant, atop a hill in western Parth Celebrant. You should speak with Doron once more.\n6\tTalk to Idmar\tIdmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant. You should bring news of your victory to Idmar.\n",
[11752]="70010168\n1\tTravel with Tordoron to Rhunendin\tTordoron is near Gath Forthnír. Tordoron has asked you to help him mount an assault against the forces of Angmar gathering in Rhunendin.\n2\tTalk to Tordoron\tTordoron is near Gath Forthnír. You should speak with Tordoron regarding your victory against the Angmarim in Rhunendin.\n",
[11753]="70030E09\n1\tClimb to the top of the Beacon of Eaworth\tThe Beacon of Eaworth is just north of the Mead Hall along the river. The timbers of the Beacon of Eaworth must be examined to ensure they are undamaged and secure.\n2\tTalk to Cendal\tCendal is at Eaworth. Report back to Cendal and inform him that the beacon appears to be structurally sound.\n",
[11754]="70019CD1\n1\tCollect bear-meat (total: 6)\tBears can be found in the dens of Brochos, which is a ways to the west of the Vineyards of Lórien. Farasdúr has asked you to hunt the bears of Brochos and return with rich meat.\n2\tTalk to Farasdúr near the Vineyards of Lórien\tFarasdúr is near the Vineyards of Lórien in Egladil, east of Brochos. You should bring the bear-meat you have collected to Farasdúr.\n",
[11755]="7006868C\n1\tTalk to Gûshida across the way from Ezôti\tA woman attending the show is trying to get your attention. Speak to the woman across the way in the Upper Ward.\n2\tTalk to Ezôti in the Upper Ward\tGûshida has asked you to pretend to befriend Ezôti in order to gain information from him. Speak to Ezôti in the Upper Ward.\n",
[11756]="7006906E\n1\tDefeat Tarasâd, the Beast of Belfalas\tFind and defeat Tarasâd, the Beast of Belfalas.\n",
[11757]="70043E03\n1\tDefend the centre of the Belegiant Bridge\tThe Belegiant Bridge is located in centre of Osgiliath over the Anduin River. You should defend the centre of the Belegiant Bridge.\n2\tKeep your post and defend the centre of the bridge\tThe Belegiant Bridge is located in the centre of Osgiliath over the Anduin River. You should keep your post and defend the centre of the Belegiant Bridge. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tListen to Grazadhal yell at you\tGrazadhal is at Dâr Dugoth. You should listen to Grazadhal yell at you.\n",
[11758]="70033C7D\n1\tDefeat Skrizg\030Defeat Tabî-kohin\tDefeat the lieutenants of the Dark Lord in Dale and ring the bells.\n",
[11759]="70033C7A\n1\tDefeat Skrizg\030Defeat Tabî-kohin\tDefeat the lieutenants of the Dark Lord in Dale and ring the bells.\n",
[11760]="70071CD3\n1\tHarvest fresh dill (total: 12)\030Collect crab claws (total: 6)\tHarvest fresh dill and collect crab claws from the ponds of Charganpâta.\n2\tReturn to Kôrzan in Sen Chatâk\tReturn to the fisher Kôrzan in Sen Chatâk with the gathered herbs and crab meat.\n",
[11761]="70052983\n1\tMilk the cows (total: 4)\tMilking cows can be found at the Beorninghús. You should milk some cows for Gírta.\n2\tChurn the milk (quantity: see journal)\tThe butter churn can be found at the Beorninghús. You should churn some milk for Gírta.\n3\tBring the butter to Gírta\tGírta can be found at the Beorninghús. You should bring the butter to Gírta.\n",
[11762]="7002EE32\n1\tAssist Lady Góda with Espying the Vale\030Assist Lady Góda with Blinding the Enemy\030Assist Lady Góda with Sowing Mayhem\030Assist Lady Góda with Evidence of Evil\tLady Góda stands near Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. Ingbert has instructed you to lend aid to Lady Góda as she plans the defence of Eaworth.\n2\tTalk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tReeve Ingbert is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale. You should return to Ingbert and let him know that Góda's preparations are complete.\n",
[11763]="7002EE43\n1\tAssist Ingmar with Espying the Vale\030Assist Ingmar with Blinding the Enemy\030Assist Ingmar with Sowing Mayhem\030Assist Ingmar with Evidence of Evil\tIngmar stands near Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. Ingbert instructed you to offer your services to his son, Ingmar, while he and Góda continue siege-preparations in Eaworth.\n2\tTalk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tIngbert is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale. You should return to Ingbert and let him know that preparations for the attack on the Orcs are complete.\n",
[11764]="70000D93\n1\tDefeat Big Black-bear\tHart Holeman's wood pile is to the north, beyond the wall and a small logging camp. Hart Holeman is willing to provide the charcoal Hyacinth Took requested, but first he wants you to drive off a big black bear that has made his wood pile its home.\n2\tTalk to Hart Holeman\tHart Holeman is at his home in the centre of Overhill. Hart Holeman had asked you to deal with the big black bear that had taken up residence in his wood pile, while he put together a parcel of charcoal for Hyacinth Took. He will be pleased to learn that the bear will no longer trouble him.\n3\tBring charcoal to Hyacinth Took\tHyacinth Took is in Tuckborough near the Great Smials. While you were away, dealing with the big black bear at Hart Holeman's wood pile, Hart was busy putting together a parcel of charcoal for you to take back to Hyacinth Took.\n",
[11765]="70022743\n1\tFind Tantafod's clutch and defeat Tantafod\tTantafod's clutch can be found on the western border of Thrór's Coomb, almost due south of Nár's Peak. Frithgeir has asked you to seek out Tantafod's clutch and destroy it. Tantafod herself may need to be dispatched as well.\n2\tFind Harcennun's clutch and defeat Harcennun\tHarcennun's clutch can be found west of Tantafod's clutch, near a large rock outcropping. Frithgeir asked you to seek out Harcennun's clutch and destroy it. You may have to dispatch Harcennun herself as well.\n3\tTalk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund\tFrithgeir is at Zudrugund within Nár's Peak, north of the gwibers' clutches. You should return to Frithgeir and tell him of your heroic deeds.\n",
[11766]="70035203\n1\tDefeat White Hand trolls (total: 3)\tTrolls can be found in Fushaum-dorám in the south-eastern Writhendowns. You should defeat the trolls.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have successfully defeated several of the White Hand trolls at Fushaum-dorám.\n",
[11767]="70024C2F\n1\tWait at Ona Kay's eating station\tThe first eating station is near Ona Kay. You should wait near the first eating station for the contest to begin.\n2\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the first station -- any foods you like.\t\n3\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the first station -- any foods you like. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n4\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the first station -- any foods you like.\t\n5\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the first station -- any foods you like.\t\n6\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the first station -- any foods you like.\t\n7\tTalk to Ona Kay\tOna Kay is near the first eating station. You should speak with Ona Kay before moving on to the next phase of the eating contest.\n",
[11768]="70024D6C\n1\tRun to the second station\tThe second station is down the stairs from the first. You should run to the second station and begin eating.\n2\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the second station -- any foods you like.\t\n3\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the second station -- any foods you like.\t\n4\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the second station -- any foods you like.\t\n5\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the second station -- any foods you like.\t\n6\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the second station -- any foods you like.\t\n7\tTalk to Freddie Symonds\tFreddie Symonds is near the second eating station. You should speak with Freddie Symonds before moving on to the next phase of the eating contest.\n",
[11769]="70024D91\n1\tRun to the third station\tThe third station is up the stairs from the second. You should run to the third station and begin eating.\n2\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the third station -- any foods you like.\t\n3\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the third station -- any foods you like.\t\n4\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the third station -- any foods you like.\t\n5\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the third station -- any foods you like.\t\n6\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the third station -- any foods you like.\t\n7\tTalk to Jack Mitford\tJack Mitford is near the third eating station. You should speak with Jack Mitford before moving on to the next phase of the eating contest.\n",
[11770]="70024D90\n1\tRun to the fourth station\tThe fourth station is down the road from the third. You should run to the fourth station and begin eating.\n2\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the fourth station -- any foods you like.\t\n3\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the fourth station -- any foods you like.\t\n4\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the fourth station -- any foods you like.\t\n5\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the fourth station -- any foods you like.\t\n6\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the fourth station -- any foods you like.\t\n7\tTalk to Nora Lewison\tNora Lewison is near the fourth eating station. You should speak with Nora Lewison before moving on to the next phase of the eating contest.\n",
[11771]="70024D93\n1\tRun to the fifth station\tThe last station is just under the bridge. You should run to the last station and begin eating.\n2\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the fifth station -- any foods you like.\t\n3\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the fifth station -- any foods you like.\t\n4\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the fifth station -- any foods you like.\t\n5\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the fifth station -- any foods you like.\t\n6\tA lovely array of different foods can be found at each eating station. You should eat five foods at the fifth station -- any foods you like.\t\n7\tTalk to Ian Prudholm\tIan Prudholm is near the fifth eating station. You should speak with Ian Prudholm before moving on to the next phase of the eating contest.\n",
[11772]="70000003\n1\tBring the recipe back to Carlo Blagrove\030Collect the yellowed recipe\tThe Great Smials are in Tuckborough, to the east of Michel Delving. The Bird and Baby Inn is in Michel Delving, to the west of Tuckborough. Carlo Blagrove has asked you to search the Great Smials for a recipe he thinks his great-grandfather might have hidden there.\n",
[11773]="700544D5\n1\tDefeat the Black Blade of Lebennin in Mordor Besieged\tIn later days, the Black Blade of Lebennin was oft-seen stalking among the hills and forests of Western Gondor, striking fear into the hearts of Men with both deadly countenance and fearsome sword. For those few who did not flee, his words poured like honey into their unwilling ears and drove them to terrible acts of evil. This may have proved his worst and most effective weapon.\n2\tDefeat the Black Blade of Lebennin in Mordor Besieged\tIn later days, the Black Blade of Lebennin was oft-seen stalking among the hills and forests of Western Gondor, striking fear into the hearts of Men with both deadly countenance and fearsome sword. For those few who did not flee, his words poured like honey into their unwilling ears and drove them to terrible acts of evil. This may have proved his worst and most effective weapon.\n3\tThe Black Blade of Lebennin, defeated but enduring\tIn later days, the Black Blade of Lebennin was oft-seen stalking among the hills and forests of Western Gondor, striking fear into the hearts of Men with both deadly countenance and fearsome sword. For those few who did not flee, his words poured like honey into their unwilling ears and drove them to terrible acts of evil. This may have proved his worst and most effective weapon.\n",
[11774]="7002C5FF\n1\tSearch for the hissing figure north-west of Ifing's location\tIfing saw a curious figure to the north-west, atop the rising slope in that direction, before he collapsed. Ifing has asked you to search to the north-west for the hissing figure he saw, if you are not too frightened to do so.\n2\tExamine the booted footprint\tA booted footprint north-west of Ifing's location, atop the rising slope, bears further investigation. Ifing was accosted by a hissing figure, and this booted footprint north-west of his location may help you find it.\n3\tTalk to Ifing\tIfing is waiting south-east of the booted footprint for you to report what you found.\n",
[11775]="7001D0CF\n1\tDefeat Black Uruks in Gathbúrz (total: 8)\tBlack Uruks can be found in Gathbúrz. Rodelleth has asked you to defeat the uruk-leaders in Gathbúrz to deplete the reserve of officers available to the Orc-forces in the battle for Mirkwood.\n2\tTalk to Rodelleth in Thangúlhad\tRodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz. You should return to Rodelleth with tidings of your victory over the Black Uruks of Mirkwood.\n",
[11776]="70059326\n1\tTalk to Supervisor Beecher\tSupervisor Beecher can be found at the Trestlespan. You should talk Supervisor Beecher.\n2\tFind black powder bombs on the Trestlespan (total: 8)\tBlack powder bombs can be found on the Trestlespan. You should remove the unlit black powder bombs as soon as you are able.\n3\tPlant black powder bombs at Norwarden (quantity: see journal)\tNorwarden can be found in the Wildwood. You should plant some of the black powder bombs that you collected at Norwarden.\n4\tPick up a nearby torch to light black powder bombs\030Light black powder bombs at Norwarden (quantity: see journal)\tNorwarden can be found in the Wildwood. You should grab a torch and light the black powder bombs that you planted.\n5\tPlant black powder bombs at Marl's Crossing (quantity: see journal)\tMarl's Crossing can be found in the Wildwood. You should plant some of the black powder bombs that you collected at Marl's Crossing.\n6\tLight black powder bombs at Marl's Crossing (quantity: see journal)\030Pick up a nearby torch to light black powder bombs\tMarl's Crossing can be found in the Wildwood. You should grab a torch and light the black powder bombs that you planted.\n7\tTalk to Aran Greenwith\tAran Greenwith can be found at Trestlebridge. You should talk to Aran Greenwith.\n8\tSurvey the reconstruction of Trestlebridge\tReconstruction work continues on Trestlebridge. You should survey the reconstruction of Trestlebridge.\n9\tTalk to Aran Greenwith\tAran Greenwith can be found at Trestlebridge. You should talk to Aran Greenwith.\n",
})
